cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "snakemake_ChIPseq: a ChIP-seq peak-calling, consensus and QC Snakemake workflow"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow for ChIP-seq analysis: human Bowtie2 alignment, filtering
  and blacklist removal, MACS2 peak calling against a matched input/IgG control
  (per-sample narrow or broad mode), IP-over-input log2 signal tracks, reproducible
  fixed-width consensus peaks with a fragment-count matrix, and a comprehensive QC
  stage with an interactive HTML report.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ji"
    family-names: "Wang"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3443-5857"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gynecoloji/snakemake_ChIPseq"
url: "https://github.com/gynecoloji/snakemake_ChIPseq"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - ChIP-seq
  - Snakemake
  - MACS2
  - consensus peaks
  - epigenomics
  - bioinformatics workflow
# `version` + `date-released` are bumped automatically by release-please on each
